FAQ

What is PiStorm3D? What is minigl.library?

PiStorm3D is a static MiniGL for PiStorm VideoCore VI. minigl.library is an OpenSource API for 3DHW on the 68k Amiga. This archive includes a version of minigl.library for PiStorm3D.

What Systems are supported by it?

Currently only Pi4/CM4/4B. Later a version for classic MiniGL-systems will as well be released (Voodoo3 etc.). An external developer is working on an OpenPCI based Radeon 9200 version.
Also Claude Schwarz is working on a version for Pi3. A (limited feature) version for Apollo Vampire is in evaluation (though the Vampire will have much lower fps and limited features).

On my system it does not run. What am I doing wrong?

Check that Picasso96API.library, rtg.library and Emulation.library all come from the same version of Picasso96. While 2D Stuff works with "mixed" installations, PiStorm3D requires all
to come from the same version. Especially effects like "green display" or "does not work in fullscreen" or "repeated crashes" are a sign of "mixed"  Picasso96 Libraries.
Use P96Version.sh to properly report, what versions you are using. Another thing you can go sure fast_page_zero is NOT activated in your config.cfg. The fast_page_zero option is NOT compatible with PiStorm 3D.
Also go sure that as to 32 Bit Screenmodes you ONLY have BGRA32 Modes enabled.

On my system Fullscreen does not work, what can I do ?

On some systems with P96 3.6.3 (though not on all such systems) Fullscreen PiStorm3D Displays only work if Picasso96/DepthIncludesAlpha is set to the value Yes.

Will PiStorm3D support PiStormPPC?

A version of minigl.library (called MiniGLWOS) for WarpOS already exists. It is only for Classic Devices (like Voodoo 3 etc.) though. Most likely the most recent version will be 
released on 8th October 2026. If a version for PiStorm3D for PiStormPPC will be recompiled will be seen in the future. 

What about support for A1200NG or THEA1200 or AmiKit ?

They are based on AmiBerry. We are in talks with the author of Amiberry (actually for the Windows/Linux/MacOS versions it alreay runs in a Beta). As to THEA1200 and A1200NG,
their manufacturers should contact us, if they want this feature. We need further information from them.

I used a game for minigl.library V27. After the public release it does not work anymore. What is the problem?

The public release version (V29) is no longer compatible to V27. The game needs to be recompiled. No Source-Code-Changes are needed, but the author of the game/port needs
to recompile with the latest SDK. This could unfortunately not be avoided.

